Nature of complaint
-------------------
{{ broker.name }} is a data broker that has failed to honor a legally mandated
personal-information deletion request after {{ attempts }} separate request(s).

Timeline
--------
- First deletion request submitted: {{ first_request_date }}
- Number of requests sent: {{ attempts }}
- Most recent verification: still listing my personal information as of {{ last_checked }}
- Reference ID: {{ reference_id }}

Legal basis
-----------
{% if broker.ccpa_compliant or person.state == 'California' -%}
Under the California Consumer Privacy Act (Cal. Civ. Code Section 1798.105), a
business must delete a consumer's personal information upon a verifiable request
and may not continue to retain or sell it. {{ broker.name }} has not complied
within the statutory 45-day window.
{%- else -%}
Under applicable state consumer-privacy law and Section 5 of the FTC Act
(unfair or deceptive practices), {{ broker.name }} is obligated to honor a
consumer deletion request and has failed to do so.
{%- endif %}

Requested relief
----------------
1. Compel {{ broker.name }} to delete all of my personal information.
2. Confirm in writing that deletion has occurred.
3. Investigate {{ broker.name }}'s handling of consumer deletion requests.

Supporting records (dates, reference IDs, and re-listing evidence) are retained
and available on request.

